ven't had any details  the office won't respond to requests for  comment and if they do have any findings  that are that are egregious you know at  the end of the day it could certainly  take a lot of money from them if there  is a civil fine but is it going to be  substantial enough to say knock them off  a billionaire's list probably not you  know you could certainly say they'd be  reputational damage but i think at this  point  you already have your opinion on donald  trump  next election fraud damage claims  a delaware county pennsylvania elections  official he oversees the voting machines  in the warehouse is suing for defamation  asking for at least fifty thousand  dollars claiming that accusations that  he tampered with the vote has impacted  his ability to do his job he's suing  trump along with some other people  involved in the campaign notably jenna  ellis and rudy giuliani  trump's attorneys have filed a  preliminary objection to the case and  the the plaintiffs are still moving  forward they're trying to get discovery  started and that is also being argued  about as well  there was a lot of um  residual damage to some people with  these election fraud claims you know  you're seeing the the overall result was  obviously  trump's out of office the election  results stood as they should have but  you know all those claims in throwing of  that mud it stuck to some people like  people who are not usually in the news  but people who work for elections boards  people who work for voting boards and  their reputation is harm and then you  know for a brief period of time a lot of  these people just got slammed online all  sorts of online abuse because they were  accused of throwing the election in  favor of joe biden and they were in  cahoots with the big state and i mean  honestly these are just people going  about in this case doing his warehouse  job  and finally cases related to january 6th  the riot at the capitol on january 6 has  led to several cases and investigations  regarding former president trump most  notably there's the house select  committee on january 6 which is  researching the causes of the event  while the committee's final result is  set to be a report on the way to that  report it has been referring some cases  to the justice department recently the  house referred two allies of former  president trump peter navarro and dan  scavino to the justice department for  defying congressional subpoenas  former president trump also faces  several lawsuits from police officers  over the january six riots the police  officers are both with the capitol  police and the metro police of dc and  they're alleging that trump inflamed  encouraged incited directed aided and  abedded the rioters who assaulted them  additionally there are two suits that  members of congress have filed against  the former president one is a group of  legislators led by karen bass the other  is representative eric swalwell and they  are alleging that there was a conspiracy  to incite a mob violating civil rights  laws most notably the ku klux klan act  of 1867 which was passed in hopes of  keeping the clan from preventing  legislators from doing their official  duties  trump's doing what trump does he is  fighting all of the allegations and  doing everything he can to slow up the  judicial process  taking his time fighting against  subpoenas and just in general not  cooperating which he doesn't really have  to he's using legal avenues to to fight  them this case this investigation is  easily the most consequential for donald  trump as you know an investigation to  trying to overturn election results  probably should be  there's probably not going to be much  impact on his businesses but this this  could potentially result in criminal  charges again that would be a long way  off if it happens at all but the general  six committee already has referred some  people over to the department of justice  [Music]
 

